From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zibao <zibaone@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 16 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] net: wireless: wire aic8800_sdio into kbuild

The Armbian 3401 patch adds drivers/net/wireless/aic8800_sdio/ but does not
touch drivers/net/wireless/{Kconfig,Makefile}. Kbuild therefore never descends
into the directory and no .ko is produced, even though the family config sets
CONFIG_AIC_SDIO_WLAN_SUPPORT=y. Add the two hook lines.

Measured on the H96 Max H618 (AIC8800D80, SDIO 0xc8a1:0x0082): the patched tree
contained the directory but the modules output had no aic8800_*.ko.

Signed-off-by: zibao <zibaone@proton.me>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/Kconfig
@@ -40,3 +40,5 @@
 source "drivers/net/wireless/virtual/Kconfig"
 
+source "drivers/net/wireless/aic8800_sdio/Kconfig"
+
 endif # WLAN
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/Makefile
@@ -23,3 +23,5 @@
 obj-$(CONFIG_WLAN_VENDOR_ZYDAS) += zydas/
 
 obj-$(CONFIG_WLAN) += virtual/
+
+obj-$(CONFIG_AIC_SDIO_WLAN_SUPPORT) += aic8800_sdio/
